From 02b7c135ae5a7796d1ead095b0118c4dc2809bea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Steven <steven@wilai.de>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 13:02:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] drm: apple: afk: reuse channel slots of disabled services

afk_recv_handle_init() only ever appended to ep->services, so a service
that went away kept its slot forever. The firmware re-announces its
services on every display power cycle, which on the AV endpoint means
two slots (DCPAVSimpleVideoInterface and DCPAVAudioInterface) per cycle
against AFK_MAX_CHANNEL == 16. After eight cycles the table is full:

  AFK[ep:29]: too many enabled services!
  AFK[ep:29]: expected announce but got 0xc0 on channel 113

and the endpoint is unusable until reboot. Seen after 13 power cycles
over five days of uptime with hdmi_audio=1, which is what makes the AV
endpoint exist in the first place - that is presumably why this has not
come up before.

afk_epic_find_service() already skips slots whose service is disabled,
so such a slot cannot be reached by channel number any more and is safe
to hand out again. Look for one before growing the array.

Note that teardown deliberately does not clear ->enabled (a reply may
still be outstanding); the flag is cleared by the service's own teardown
op, so only slots the service layer has finished with are reused.

Signed-off-by: Steven <steven@wilai.de>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c
index b7f162988269..99617e8c57f2 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/afk.c
@@ -259,7 +259,19 @@ static void afk_recv_handle_init(struct apple_dcp_afkep *ep, u32 channel,
 		return;
 	}
 
-	if (ep->num_channels >= AFK_MAX_CHANNEL) {
+	/*
+	 * Look for a slot whose service has been disabled and reuse it. The
+	 * firmware re-announces its services on every display power cycle,
+	 * and ->num_channels only ever grew, so ep->services filled up after
+	 * a handful of cycles and every announce from then on was rejected.
+	 * afk_epic_find_service() skips disabled slots, so nothing can still
+	 * reach one by channel number.
+	 */
+	for (ch_idx = 0; ch_idx < ep->num_channels; ch_idx++)
+		if (!ep->services[ch_idx].enabled)
+			break;
+
+	if (ch_idx == ep->num_channels && ep->num_channels >= AFK_MAX_CHANNEL) {
 		dev_err(ep->dcp->dev, "AFK[ep:%02x]: too many enabled services!\n",
 			ep->endpoint);
 		return;
@@ -305,7 +317,8 @@ static void afk_recv_handle_init(struct apple_dcp_afkep *ep, u32 channel,
 		goto free;
 	}
 
-	ch_idx = ep->num_channels++;
+	if (ch_idx == ep->num_channels)
+		ep->num_channels++;
 	spin_lock_init(&ep->services[ch_idx].lock);
 	ep->services[ch_idx].enabled = true;
 	ep->services[ch_idx].torndown = false;
